{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1220600-mage-combat-blenders","id":1220600,"title":"Mage Combat Blenders","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-20T12:06:08-07:00","id":1220600,"title":"Mage Combat Blenders","content":"Using normal character generation rules, pitch an especially powerful starting PC. There's no need to fully stat them out; simply addressing the powerful points and combinations will do in most cases.<br /> <br /> One example might be an Etherite built (mechanically at least) around the Hands of Daedalus merit.<br /> <br /> This 3 point Merit gives -2 difficulty when working with mechanisms and crafting, and turns all of the items you spend time developing familiarity with into Unique Personalized Instruments (giving -2 difficulty to Arete rolls where they are the instrument). Build your focus around instruments and practices which can benefit from this, from hypertech jetpacks to muscle cars to energy weapons and cybernetics. Invest enough points in Abilities to cover these various instruments (some Drive, some Energy Weapons, Craft, Tech and Hypertech).<br /> <br /> Take Forces 2 (Damage) and Prime 3 (Charms, Aggravated damage and access to energy). Using a personalized car as a focus, for example, the Etherite could perform a coincidental Forces 2 Prime 3 effect to obliterate whatever or whoever they crash into (inflicting Aggravated damage)... Difficulty 5 base, pushed down to 3 automatically. 2-3 successes on average means 6 or 8 points of Aggravated damage; even if our target is a Garou, they're at death's door. The mechanics would be identical if they were using a modified taser... which would probably be a lot more convenient than attacking using a vehicle, which draws a lot of attention and risks crashing.<br /> <br /> This leaves a lot of room for effects outside of &quot;kill it to death&quot;... they still have another Sphere dot to allocate, and Forces + Prime leaves room for damage resistance, flying, weather control, Wonder development...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T06:28:17-07:00","id":1220811,"title":"","content":"Likely a more efficient route; start with &quot;natural&quot; Aggravated damage and focus on applying it as efficiently as possible.<br /> <br /> So using Advantages, start with Aggravated Damage claws. Perhaps your father was Fenrir, of Norse myth. That's a 6 point Advantage. Now invest in Brawl 5, Dexterity 5, Strength 5, and make Fenrir a 5 dot Totem for +3 Brawl (along with advice, a potent ally, some Esoterica and Cosmology)...<br /> <br /> Now use level 1 Sphere effects to lower Difficulty for your Brawl attacks. With 13 dice on an attack, rolling at Difficulty 3 with Exploding 10s (highly achievable), you can achieve 10.4 successes on average. That's 5 (Strength) + 9 (Extra Successes) + 1 (Claws) dice of Aggravated damage. That's 6-7 points of Aggravated damage on a modest roll. Spending a few Freebies or EXP for an extra Spec would make it 7-8 points on a modest roll.<br /> <br /> Combining with Time 3 could make this exceptionally dangerous. A Forces 2 attack can only happen once per turn, but if such a Mage were to take Extra Actions (having cast their difficulty reduction Effect at the start of the night as an extended action) then they would be able to take out several foes in a single turn.<br /> <br /> For example, at the start of the scene they could use Time 2 / Entropy 1 / Correspondence 1 to map out the movements and probabilities of the people in the room, predicting their movements in advance (to reduce attack difficulties). They could then implement a Time 3 effect and strike up to 4 people lethally in a single round (1 action, plus up to 3 actions from the Arete roll).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T19:55:45-07:00","id":1221046,"title":"","content":"I built a rather effective orphan with Life 3, Forces 2, Mind 1 and a blessing of an always on (as in can\u2019t turn it off) perception of and ability to touch (and be touched) by wraiths. They awakened while they were a victim of a mass sacrifice by a death cult, only the death didn\u2019t stick and they came back empowered by the souls of every last murder victim with them (these collective voices are their avatar).<br /> <br /> Their paradigm is that the living draw strength from the dead and the dead from the living (from keeping their memories alive and resolving their troubles). Life 3 grants them the ability to basically be The Crow. Forces 2 grants both stealth and various poltergeist-like abilities (moving objects, flickering lights/electronic control, shadows moving of their own accord, chill breezes, etc.). Mind 1 and the unbondable merit reflect the fact that their head is already filled with a hundred angry ghosts... there\u2019s just not room for anything else up there... multitasking is literally asking one of the ghosts in their head to work on a particular problem instead of doing it themselves. The \u2018death sight\u2019 and \u2018touch\u2019 were bought as blessings instead of spheres because they were intended to be always on and not under the character\u2019s control.<br /> <br /> They made a mission of putting the restless dead, particularly murder victims, to rest by resolving their issues. Often this involves meting out justice to supernatural monsters that prey upon the innocent.<br /> <br /> Before awakening the character had been part of an extremely wealthy British family. The cultists killed their entire family though so they sold off the mansion and other assets and now lives on a sizable yacht, both because it provides a mobile base of operations and as a respite from the calls of the restless dead (not many can reach them when they\u2019re out at sea).<br /> <br /> They\u2019ve learned to fight from various ghost mentors and they\u2019ve used their resources to pick up armor, weapons and other gear useful to hunting down monsters human and otherwise. They\u2019ve learned that much of ghostly aid they receive is easier for them to call upon when they dress the part of a \u201ccostumed\u201d vigilante (a mythic thread in the vein of the Shadow, the Crow, Blade, Selene from Underworld, etc.) and has puzzled out that \u201cghosts\u201d have an easier time acting on the world when their actions can be cloaked in coincidence. Paradox Backlash, when it comes, is in the form of hostile poltergeist activity near them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T04:18:43-07:00","id":1221446,"title":"","content":"Be an Akashic Brother, take as much Do as GM lets you, get the one that reduces weapon difficulty. Buy yourself a Sword of Mars talisman from Forged by Dragon Fire - get -3 difficulty reduction on attack and damage rolls. Take Graceful merit from Sorcerer's Crusade Companion, which gives -1 dif on Dexterity rolls. Now you are at -5 difficulty to your stabbing and parrying rolls. Take Prime 2 to have Aggravated damage. Take Life 3 to soak Aggravated damage and buff Dexterity. Buy a tattoo wonder that gives you extra actions. Doesn't really matter what your third sphere is, but Entropy and Correspondence are good picks. Buy Arcane 5 and Stealth 3.<br /> <br /> Start each month with a ritual that gives you 5 in Dex, Stamina and Strength and lets you soak Aggravated. You now have 7 dice to hit things at average difficulty of 1, 13 dice to sneak up on things at -1 difficulty (before magic), soak aggravated damage. Your damage rolls have -3 difficulty and are Aggravated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 05-23-2018, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T04:38:00-07:00","id":1221448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1220600-mage-combat-blenders?p=1221446#post1221446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Be an Akashic Brother, take as much Do as GM lets you, get the one that reduces weapon difficulty. Buy yourself a Sword of Mars talisman from Forged by Dragon Fire - get -3 difficulty reduction on attack and damage rolls. Take Graceful merit from Sorcerer's Crusade Companion, which gives -1 dif on Dexterity rolls. Now you are at -5 difficulty to your stabbing and parrying rolls. Take Prime 2 to have Aggravated damage. Take Life 3 to soak Aggravated damage and buff Dexterity. Buy a tattoo wonder that gives you extra actions. Doesn't really matter what your third sphere is, but Entropy and Correspondence are good picks. Buy Arcane 5 and Stealth 3.<br /> <br /> Start each month with a ritual that gives you 5 in Dex, Stamina and Strength and lets you soak Aggravated. You now have 7 dice to hit things at average difficulty of 1, 13 dice to sneak up on things at -1 difficulty (before magic), soak aggravated damage. Your damage rolls have -3 difficulty and are Aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can difficulties for mundane actions be reduced to 1? I'm actually not sure. Is 2 the minimum?<br /> <br /> As for the rest of it, it wouldn't cost that much to have Melee 5, which would mean 10 dice to hit. And at that point... well with Exploding 10s and a difficulty of 1 or 2, we're looking at 9 or more successes. Since it's an ambush, no dodge. And then with Strength 5 and +2 damage from the sword, we're inflicting 15 dice of Aggravated damage at difficulty 3... Which is 12 points of Aggravated damage. Which is a lot. And then there's multiple actions... oh dear...<br /> <br /> In terms of developing this further, Iron Shirt (from the Do powers list) would make them an unstoppable tank too. Stamina 5, plus all of your points in Do, plus any Armour you're wearing, could mean a Soak pool great enough to shrug off any Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> And lastly, there are maneuvers in M20 for fighting which aren't really usable because they increase the difficulty by 1 or 2, however with this much difficulty reduction such a Mage could just abuse those maneuvers to stun their opponent or gain advantages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-23-2018, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T10:32:52-07:00","id":1221497,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the minimum difficulty is 3, in any circumstance. There's no sense in lowering the difficulty any further, mechanically. Also, even very trivial things may not go exactly as planned (I'm not saying you botch them, but you may not have as many successes as you really hoped for).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T10:46:25-07:00","id":1221500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1220600-mage-combat-blenders?p=1221497#post1221497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the minimum difficulty is 3, in any circumstance. There's no sense in lowering the difficulty any further, mechanically. Also, even very trivial things may not go exactly as planned (I'm not saying you botch them, but you may not have as many successes as you really hoped for).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in that case, you could economize on certain difficulty-reducing traits. You'll almost never need more than -4 difficulty (enough to push a Difficulty 7 interaction down to Difficulty 3). Once you've got enough Difficulty modifiers to always hit Difficulty 3 on certain critical rolls, the best investment is more dice. At low difficulties extra dice are a great investment.<br /> <br /> I find it interesting actually. Mechanically speaking VTM has a LOT of ways of gaining more dice very easily. Blood pumping and the Physical Disciplines are obvious examples. Mage is filled with Difficulty reductions, but gaining dice seems less common. And there's definitely a useful middleground if you want the best result possible. If you've got Arete 1-3 (or your Attribute + Ability pool isn't very impressive), then reducing Difficulty will only do so much. It makes it much safer, but you won't get the insane results you might hope for. This Difficulty vs. Dice relationship makes traits like Cult and Stamina quite useful, since you can abuse a low difficulty simply by repeating the roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-23-2018, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T20:14:46-07:00","id":1221604,"title":"","content":"You can bring the difficulty down to 2. Its arete rolls that can go no lower than 3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T10:46:16-07:00","id":1221761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1220600-mage-combat-blenders?p=1221604#post1221604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can bring the difficulty down to 2. Its arete rolls that can go no lower than 3</div> </div> </div> </div>Arete rolls can go down <i>no more than by</i> 3. Very important distinction. You can have dif 2 arete roll, but a dif 9 arete roll can't ever go down to dif 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T11:34:05-07:00","id":1221777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1220600-mage-combat-blenders?p=1221761#post1221761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arete rolls can go down <i>no more than by</i> 3. Very important distinction. You can have dif 2 arete roll, but a dif 9 arete roll can't ever go down to dif 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Difficulty Modifiers chart for magick states that there's a minimum difficulty of 3 and a maximum difficulty of 10 (and then explains the optional Thresholds system, where the maximum difficulty is 9).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T03:58:08-07:00","id":1222201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1220600-mage-combat-blenders?p=1220811#post1220811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likely a more efficient route; start with &quot;natural&quot; Aggravated damage and focus on applying it as efficiently as possible.<br /> <br /> So using Advantages, start with Aggravated Damage claws. Perhaps your father was Fenrir, of Norse myth. That's a 6 point Advantage. Now invest in Brawl 5, Dexterity 5, Strength 5, and make Fenrir a 5 dot Totem for +3 Brawl (along with advice, a potent ally, some Esoterica and Cosmology)...<br /> <br /> Now use level 1 Sphere effects to lower Difficulty for your Brawl attacks. With 13 dice on an attack, rolling at Difficulty 3 with Exploding 10s (highly achievable), you can achieve 10.4 successes on average. That's 5 (Strength) + 9 (Extra Successes) + 1 (Claws) dice of Aggravated damage. That's 6-7 points of Aggravated damage on a modest roll. Spending a few Freebies or EXP for an extra Spec would make it 7-8 points on a modest roll.<br /> <br /> Combining with Time 3 could make this exceptionally dangerous. A Forces 2 attack can only happen once per turn, but if such a Mage were to take Extra Actions (having cast their difficulty reduction Effect at the start of the night as an extended action) then they would be able to take out several foes in a single turn.<br /> <br /> For example, at the start of the scene they could use Time 2 / Entropy 1 / Correspondence 1 to map out the movements and probabilities of the people in the room, predicting their movements in advance (to reduce attack difficulties). They could then implement a Time 3 effect and strike up to 4 people lethally in a single round (1 action, plus up to 3 actions from the Arete roll).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, similar minds I see. I was thinking along the same lines when designing a close quarters fighter. However, niphilim is a 7 point merit, not 6. However you can also take 7 dots in traits for 5pt mental derangement. if you take Beast Inside as a drawback you can go at around dexterity 10, strength 4, stamina 3. then invest in either Deviant Heart or Werewolf Paw wonders. Put 4 pt in arete for arete 2, prime 2, spirit 2. life 2, Now you can make an awakened spirit weapon that deals aggravated damage for free and adds bonuses from spirit help. do same with armor. use life 2, prime 2 to buff yourself farther. use 7 daily vis to buy more weapons or pay spirits for help. At this level you can also make talens, like ones that allow extra actions, heal or give bonus to fighting without exp or freebe spent. Pretty sure at this level you can take down a garou or HIT mark in face-to-face fight without much trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 05-26-2018, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T04:05:01-07:00","id":1222202,"title":"","content":"Now that I think, some of the most powerful would be a starting Werbana/Progenitor with specialty in bioengineering viruses and summoning disease spirits at the same time. Something like 5 in intelligence, blatancy, occult and bioengineering. 3 life/3 spirit and cult 5 for ritual magic. maybe also self confident and strength I adversity to really own the long game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 05-26-2018, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T05:40:04-07:00","id":1222217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1220600-mage-combat-blenders?p=1221761#post1221761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arete rolls can go down <i>no more than by</i> 3. Very important distinction. You can have dif 2 arete roll, but a dif 9 arete roll can't ever go down to dif 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh and further to the minimum difficulty being 3 (to be clear, Arete rolls are difficulty 3 minimum), an important qualifier to the first part is that they can't go down by more than 3 from the base difficulty. So if the base difficulty is 7, then the minimum difficulty is 4, even if the difficulty is raised to 9 by something else first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-26-2018, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T05:48:40-07:00","id":1222220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1220600-mage-combat-blenders?p=1222201#post1222201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, similar minds I see. I was thinking along the same lines when designing a close quarters fighter. However, niphilim is a 7 point merit, not 6. However you can also take 7 dots in traits for 5pt mental derangement. if you take Beast Inside as a drawback you can go at around dexterity 10, strength 4, stamina 3. then invest in either Deviant Heart or Werewolf Paw wonders. Put 4 pt in arete for arete 2, prime 2, spirit 2. life 2, Now you can make an awakened spirit weapon that deals aggravated damage for free and adds bonuses from spirit help. do same with armor. use life 2, prime 2 to buff yourself farther. use 7 daily vis to buy more weapons or pay spirits for help. At this level you can also make talens, like ones that allow extra actions, heal or give bonus to fighting without exp or freebe spent. Pretty sure at this level you can take down a garou or HIT mark in face-to-face fight without much trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I wonder if we've run out of points at this point? Also, I'm assuming you mean Arete 3, not 4 (3 is the maximum at character generation, because they don't want Mages with 4 dots in a Sphere, or players avoiding all of the Seekings they need to do by starting at 4 or 5).<br /> <br /> The advantage, for me personally, of the whole Niphilim thing is that your source of Aggravated damage won't be lost if Judgement spirits you away, or if you're teleported into the 17th inverse of the 8th circle, or if you're captured by the Technocracy and thrown into a cell. The fact that you can pop aggravated claws whenever you need to, and stealthily kill with them, is a big edge. Hiding the Sword of Ultimate Legend is probably trickier.<br /> <br /> If a mega-combat-blender is built around a really powerful item, like a sword or a wolf's paw, then it might be a good idea to have it so that you draw it out of the Umbra, or out of a safe place using Correspondence. In fact, any character built around a powerful item (such as a potent Fetish, Wonder or Phylactery) should probably have some Correspondence to be safe. Besides, a combat-blender who can learn to teleport behind you can pull a &quot;nothing personel kid&quot; which is something I've always wanted to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-26-2018, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}